# The DLLs in this tree are DELIVERABLES and are committed on purpose, so that
# nobody installing an addon or a plugin needs a compiler:
#
#   lua/worlddraw.dll                  the engine
#   daemon/worlddraw_daemon.dll        the hook daemon
#   lua/worlddrawdemo/libs/*.dll       the demo addon, ready to copy and load
#   example/example.dll                the demo plugin
#   example/worlddraw_daemon.dll       the daemon that ships beside it
#
# Only intermediates and diagnostics are ignored.

# Object files. Every build script removes its own; this is the backstop.
*.o

# Harness and tool output directories (tools/*/build).
build/

# The render-thread probe image from lua/build-probe.sh. A diagnostic build,
# not part of the kit, and never deployed to a player.
lua/worlddraw_probe.dll

# Working notes, not deliverables: the design record and the render-thread
# probe's operating note are for developing this library, not for the people
# installing it. They stay out of the shipped tree.
lua/DESIGN.md
lua/PROBE.md
lua/build-probe.sh

# Python bytecode from the build gates.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
